  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Claude Go-To home">
        <span class="brand-mark"><img src="assets/compass-mark.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32" /></span>
        <span>Claude <strong>Go-To</strong></span>
      </a>
      <div class="header-actions">
        <nav id="site-nav" class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
          <a href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a>
          <a href="#lessons">Lessons</a>
          <a href="#assessment">Assessment</a>
          <a data-github-link href="https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/claude-go-to">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </nav>
        <button id="theme-toggle" class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to light theme" aria-pressed="false">
          <span class="theme-icon theme-sun" aria-hidden="true">☀</span>
          <span class="theme-icon theme-moon" aria-hidden="true">☾</span>
          <span class="theme-label">Theme</span>
        </button>
        <button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-controls="site-nav" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="sr-only">Open navigation</span><span></span><span></span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section id="top" class="hero section-shell">
        <div class="hero-copy reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> An independent learning resource</p>
          <h1>Build an AI workflow your <em>whole team</em> can trust.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Claude Go-To turns scattered prompts and one-off experiments into a calm, repeatable
            system for planning, building, reviewing, and shipping software.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="#roadmap">Choose your path <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a class="text-link" href="#lessons">Explore the lessons <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-proof" aria-label="Project highlights">
            <div><strong>10</strong><span>hands-on modules</span></div>
            <div><strong>0</strong><span>dependencies to install</span></div>
            <div><strong>∞</strong><span>room to make it yours</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual reveal reveal-delay" aria-label="Example AI development workflow">
          <div class="workspace-window">
            <div class="window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><p>claude-go-to / workflow</p><i>● Live</i></div>
            <div class="workspace-body">
              <aside class="workspace-sidebar">
                <small>WORKSPACE</small>
                <p class="active"><b>◇</b> New feature</p>
                <p><b>□</b> Context</p>
                <p><b>△</b> Review</p>
                <p><b>○</b> Release</p>
              </aside>
              <div class="workspace-main">
                <p class="code-label">/delivery-plan</p>
                <h2>Ship a change with clarity.</h2>
                <p>Explore the codebase, agree the plan, validate the work, then leave a useful handoff.</p>
                <div class="workflow-list">
                  <div><span>01</span><b>Map the change</b><i>complete</i></div>
                  <div><span>02</span><b>Build in a clear boundary</b><i>in progress</i></div>
                  <div><span>03</span><b>Run focused checks</b><i>queued</i></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="floating-note"><span>✦</span><p>Make the good path<br /><strong>the easy path.</strong></p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="value-strip">
        <div class="section-shell value-inner">
          <p>From an empty prompt</p><span>→</span><p>to a visible system</p><span>→</span><p>to confident delivery</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="roadmap" class="section-shell roadmap">
        <div class="section-intro reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Find your starting point</p>
          <h2>Start where the friction is.</h2>
          <p>Pick the path that solves your next real problem—not the one that tries to teach everything at once.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-layout">
          <div class="path-tabs reveal" role="tablist" aria-label="Learning paths">
            <button class="path-card is-selected" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-path="beginner">
              <span class="path-number">01</span><span><strong>Foundation</strong><small>Prompts and context</small></span><b>→</b>
            </button>
            <button class="path-card" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-path="intermediate">
              <span class="path-number">02</span><span><strong>Practice</strong><small>Skills and quality gates</small></span><b>→</b>
            </button>
            <button class="path-card" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-path="advanced">
              <span class="path-number">03</span><span><strong>Systems</strong><small>Agents and delivery loops</small></span><b>→</b>
            </button>
          </div>
          <div id="path-detail" class="path-detail reveal" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="lessons" class="lessons-section">
        <div class="section-shell">
          <div class="lessons-heading reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">The field guide</p>
              <h2>A small set of skills. A meaningful difference.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Each lesson is short, concrete, and designed to leave you with something useful in your repository.</p>
          </div>
          <div id="module-grid" class="module-grid"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-shell operating-system">
        <div class="operating-copy reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">A calm operating system</p>
          <h2>Good AI work is still good engineering.</h2>
          <p>Useful context, focused boundaries, small checks, and clear decisions matter just as much as the model you use.</p>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="guides/09-delivery-systems.md">Read the delivery guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="principles reveal reveal-delay">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Make context visible</h3><p>Write down what a new teammate would need to act safely.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Keep scope deliberate</h3><p>Give each prompt, skill, or role a clear boundary and outcome.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Check at the right moment</h3><p>Run the smallest useful validation before the change becomes expensive.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="assessment" class="assessment-section">
        <div class="section-shell assessment-layout">
          <div class="assessment-copy reveal">
            <p class="eyebrow">Quick self-assessment</p>
            <h2>What would make your next task easier?</h2>
            <p>Three quick answers point you to the most valuable next lesson.</p>
          </div>
          <form id="assessment-form" class="assessment-card reveal reveal-delay">
            <fieldset>
              <legend>Do you keep project instructions in one shared place?</legend>
              <label><input type="radio" name="context" value="0" /> Not yet</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="context" value="1" /> Yes, consistently</label>
            </fieldset>
            <fieldset>
              <legend>Do your repeated tasks have a reusable method?</legend>
              <label><input type="radio" name="repeat" value="0" /> Usually not</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="repeat" value="1" /> Yes, for most work</label>
            </fieldset>
            <fieldset>
              <legend>Does independent work have a clear review step?</legend>
              <label><input type="radio" name="agents" value="0" /> Not reliably</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="agents" value="1" /> Yes</label>
            </fieldset>
            <div class="assessment-action">
              <button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Get my recommendation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
              <p id="assessment-result" aria-live="polite"></p>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-shell launch-section reveal">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Open source and yours to adapt</p>
          <h2>Turn this guide into your team’s go-to playbook.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="launch-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" data-github-link href="https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/claude-go-to">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="GITHUB_SETUP.md">Publish your own version <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

